p.src:
Return now to the detector. Let $\ket{+}$ denote its up state and $\ket{-}$ its down state. A general spin state is a linear combination $\ket\psi=a_+\ket{+}+a_-\ket{-}
  \quad\longleftrightarrow\quad
  \begin{pmatrix}a_+\\a_-\end{pmatrix}.$ The plus and minus signs inside the kets are labels, not arithmetic operations. Once this ordered basis is chosen, $\ket{+}=
  \begin{pmatrix}1\\0\end{pmatrix},
  \qquad
  \ket{-}=
  \begin{pmatrix}0\\1\end{pmatrix}.$ Indeed, $a_+\begin{pmatrix}1\\0\end{pmatrix}
  +a_-\begin{pmatrix}0\\1\end{pmatrix}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}a_+\\a_-\end{pmatrix}.$

